# The optional `[features]` flags, as Settings > General lists them.

features-acp-chats = ACP chats
features-acp-chats-description = Show sheprd-acp chats as native chat views and offer new chats with the agents installed on the host. Off, chat panes keep their terminal and nothing looks for sheprd-acp or agents.
features-mcp = MCP server
features-mcp-description = Let MCP clients such as Claude Desktop, Cursor, or Codex use Sheprd through `sheprd mcp`: its windows and tabs, pages and your notes on them, worktrees, pull requests, memory, and checkpoints. Restoring a checkpoint, creating a worktree, fanning out, and teleporting open a dialog here for you to confirm; opening pages and files, worktree notes, and repository memory (adding, pinning, and forgetting entries) change without asking, as the sheprd command does. Run `sheprd mcp config` for the setting to paste into a client.
features-moonframe-window = Moonframe window (beta)
features-moonframe-window-description = Open Sheprd in its new window, laid out in Luau with Moonframe. It is in beta: turn it off if something is missing or wrong, and Sheprd opens its classic window. Takes effect the next time Sheprd starts. On macOS, hold ⌥ Option as Sheprd starts to open the other window once.
features-qa-menu = QA menu
features-qa-menu-description = Add a QA menu for checking the app by hand: sample toasts and dialogs, update progress, sounds, a test notification, the badge, and slowed animations.
features-sidebar-hover-menu = Open space menus on hover
features-sidebar-hover-menu-description = Open a space's menu when the pointer rests on its sidebar row, without a right click. Moving the pointer anywhere but into that menu closes it again.
